# DAY 4 — Spot CRUD, Search, Save, Seed Script

**Date:** August 3, 2026  
**Status:** ✅ Complete  
**Progress Jump:** 15% → 50%

## What I Learned

### CRUD Operations
Create, Read, Update, Delete — the four basic operations for any resource.

### Route Ordering in FastAPI
FastAPI matches routes top-to-bottom. `/search/` must come before `/{id}` because `{id}` is a wildcard that matches anything.

### ILIKE for Search
Case-insensitive pattern matching in SQL. `ILIKE '%cafe%'` matches "Cafe", "CAFE", "cafes".

### Authorization vs Authentication
- Authentication = Who are you? (login)
- Authorization = Are you allowed to do this? (only creator can delete their spot)

### Save/Bookmark Pattern
Many-to-many relationship. One user saves many spots. One spot saved by many users. Requires a join table (`saved_spots`).

### Seed Script
A Python script that populates the database with initial data. Useful for testing and demo.

